An atom emitted by two files appears once. A bundle keeps its rules together,
in block order.

  $ cat > a.ml <<EOT
  > [@@@css.atoms [
  >   ("_shared", ["._shared{color:red}"], 1, 0, 1, []);
  >   ("_bundle", ["._bundle{a:b}"; "._bundle:hover{a:c}"], 1, 0, 2, [])
  > ]]
  > EOT

  $ cat > b.ml <<EOT
  > [@@@css.atoms [
  >   ("_shared", ["._shared{color:red}"], 1, 0, 1, []);
  >   ("_bundle", ["._bundle{a:b}"; "._bundle:hover{a:c}"], 1, 0, 2, [])
  > ]]
  > EOT

  $ styled-ppx.generate a.ml b.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._bundle{a:b}
  ._bundle:hover{a:c}
  ._shared{color:red}
